# Test: ze bgp decode shows the Binding SID sub-TLV of a received SR Policy
# VALIDATES: a type-13 Binding SID sub-TLV of Length 18 is shown as the SRv6 SID it
#            carries; one of Length 20 holding the same SID is shown malformed.
# PREVENTS: a received SRv6 BSID shown only as raw attribute hex, or a sub-TLV of a
#           length RFC 9830 does not define read as an SRv6 SID.
# RFC 9830 Section 2.4.2: "If the length is 18, then the BSID contains a 16-octet
# SRv6 SID."
stdin=good:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF0075020000005E4001010040020040050400000064800E1600014904C0000201006000000000000000640A000001C01734000F00300C060000000000640D12000020010DB80000000000000000000000B58000110009060000000000010106000003E81000
stdin=long:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF007702000000604001010040020040050400000064800E1600014904C0000201006000000000000000640A000001C01736000F00320C060000000000640D14000020010DB80000000000000000000000B500008000110009060000000000010106000003E81000
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze bgp decode --json --family ipv4/sr-policy -:stdin=good
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains={"flags":0,"name":"binding-sid","srv6-sid":"2001:db8::b5","type":13}
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze bgp decode --json --family ipv4/sr-policy -:stdin=long
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains={"malformed":true,"name":"binding-sid","type":13,"value":"000020010db80000000000000000000000b50000"}
